  "_notes": {
   "Gold is king": "Gold does everything - training, building, upgrading. Collectors are slow; raiding is the fast path. Creates PvP pressure naturally.",
   "Oil creates real stakes": "Oil is consumed every time you deploy vehicles on a raid. No Oil = no attack. A well-raided base loses its ability to retaliate. Forces active play.",
   "Steel is the long game": "Steel upgrades are expensive and slow. A base with maxed Steel Depots is a high-value target. Supply lines matter.",
   "Steal percentages": "Attacker steals 20% Gold, 25% Oil (most exposed), 15% Steel of the LOOTABLE amount in storage, limited by the Loot Cap for the defender's CC (see Economy Monetization workbook). Oil Tanks have the lowest HP.",
   "No premium resource": "Gold, Oil and Steel are earned through play only. A premium currency (War Bonds) is added in the Economy and Monetization workbook; it never replaces earned resources."
  }
